	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_type">
		<text>Perk type</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_type_desc">
		<text>A perk can be of three types:
		\n- %c[orange]ARCHETYPE%c[white]: a full fledged class perk with active feats. NPCs have a chance to spawn with it and only with one.
		\n- %c[orange]MAIN%c[white]: a major perk with one or more feats. Might have active feat. NPCs can have at most 2 main perks.  
		\n- %c[orange]SECONDARY%c[white]: a minor perk with a single feat, that cannot be active. NPC always have 2 secondary perks.
		</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_category">
		<text>Perk category</text>
	</string>	
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_category_desc">
		<text>The perk category might detrmine which main perks an NPC can have. 
		\n Main perks must be of the same category of the archetype perk if an NPC has one.</text>
	</string>			
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_chance">
		<text>Perk chance</text>
	</string>	
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_chance_desc">
		<text>Chance for an NPC to spawn with this perk. The value as a percentage.</text>
	</string>	
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_enabled">
		<text>Enabled</text>
	</string>	
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_perk_enabled_desc">
		<text>Enables the registration of this perk. If set to no, an npc that has this perk will not use this perk and its feats. The actor also won't benefit from it as well. You must reload the game for this change to be in effect.</text>
	</string>	
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_feat_type">
		<text>Feat type</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_feat_type_desc">
		<text>A feat can be of several types:
		\n- %c[orange]ACTIVE%c[white]: an active feat is activated on player command or automatically by the npc ai. It might have a cooldown and use the actionbar keybind for the activation. 
		\n- %c[orange]PASSIVE%c[white]: a passive feat is activated by a context (game events, stances, etc). For instance opening a stash, buying from an npc, aiming with a scope, etc. 
		\n- %c[orange]BOON%c[white]: a one-time reward/boon that is given to the npc upon rolling this perk. NPC can have only have 1 boon.
		\n- %c[orange]TRAIT%c[white]: a feat with both positive and negative effects. NPC can have only have 1 trait.
		\n- %c[orange]MUTATION%c[white]: a feat that affects another feat, mainly by changing its properties and effects.				
		</text>
	</string>	
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_feat_mode">
		<text>Feat mode</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_st_npcd_feat_mode_desc">
		<text>A feat can mode can be of several types:
		\n- %c[orange]AUTO%c[white]: automatically activated based by the npc ai as implemented in the feat. The effect is %c[green]applied%c[white] upon activation and it has a cooldown.
		\n- %c[orange]MANUAL%c[white]: manually activated by the player with an input key. The effect is %c[green]applied%c[white] upon activation and it has a cooldown.
		\n- %c[orange]MODAL%c[white]: manually activated by the player with an input key. The effect is %c[green]applied%c[white] if the modal is on, disabled when it's off.
		\n- %c[orange]EVENT%c[white]: activated upon one or more in-game context occurs. The effect is %c[yellow]evaluated%c[white] following activation.
		\n- %c[orange]STANCE%c[white]: Stance is a special case of Event mode. Activation is available when the player enters a particular stance, and activation happens when one or more contexts occurs. The effect is %c[yellow]evaluated%c[white] only following activation and not stance entering.
		\n- %c[orange]CUSTOM%c[white]: A custom activation mechanism defined by the perk's implementation.
		</text>
	</string>	
